Errors are on scores standardised with the training fold's mean and standard deviation: the error of a model is its mean squared error over the target benchmarks, and we report the root of the mean over test models (standardised RMSE) and use the squared version for closure. Three references bracket it. The \emph{column mean} predicts the training mean (floor); the \emph{leave-one-benchmark-out} (LOBO) reference predicts each target from all other $N-1$ benchmarks of the new model (the lower error of the factor-model and Ledoit--Wolf conditional predictors); the \emph{in-sample} fit sees the test model's targets and is drawn only as a labelled, optimistic bound. The \emph{closure}
\begin{equation}
C(k)=\frac{E_{\rm colmean}-E_k}{E_{\rm colmean}-E_{\rm LOBO}},\qquad k^*(c)=\min\{k: C(k)\ge c\},
