\paragraph{The Chernoff remark.}
With $X_i=A^{-1/2}b_{J_i}b_{J_i}^\top A^{-1/2}\succeq0$ for $J_i$ uniform and independent, $\lambda_{\max}(X_i)\le\ell_{\max}=\max_j\ell_j=\mu_{\rm coh}r/N$ and $\mathbb{E}X_i=I/N$, so $\lambda_{\min}(\sum_i\mathbb{E}X_i)=k/N$. Remark~5.3 of \citet{tropp2012user} with $t=1-\varepsilon$ gives $\mathbb{P}\{\lambda_{\min}(\sum_iX_i)\le(1-\varepsilon)k/N\}\le r\exp(-\varepsilon^2k/(2\mu_{\rm coh}r))$. This is at most $\eta$ iff $k\ge2\mu_{\rm coh}r\log(r/\eta)/\varepsilon^2$, and on the complement $\Sigma_S\preceq(I+(1-\varepsilon)\tfrac{k}{N}A)^{-1}$, so the reducible risk is bounded by $\mathrm{tr}(W(I+(1-\varepsilon)\tfrac{k}{N}A)^{-1}W^\top)$ (a superset of columns adds positive terms). Two limits apply. The bound is for draws with replacement; the sum over the distinct set is at most that over the multiset, so it does not by itself bound the without-replacement case, for which \citet{gross2010note} would be needed (we read only its abstract); we therefore tested the without-replacement case numerically: over 2\,000 draws per $k$ on the fitted loadings, the share of draws violating the eigenvalue event never exceeded the Chernoff value (35 of 35 rows), which is a check and not a proof. And it is vacuous: with $\varepsilon=0.5,\eta=0.1$ the sufficient $k$ is 551 (MTEB-Eng, $N=70$), 742 (MTEB-Multi, $N=247$), 57 (HELM MMLU, $N=57$) and 459 (synthetic, $N=60$), and the risk bound is below the measured mean for $k<8$--10 on the MTEB pools and 1.6--3.2 times above it at $k=30$. The Jensen lower bound held in all 35 rows.

